<title>LEBANON: Lebanon issues 17 billion pounds of 60-day CDs.</title>
<headline>Lebanon issues 17 billion pounds of 60-day CDs.</headline>
<dateline>BEIRUT 1997-07-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of Lebanon said on Thursday it issued certificates of deposit dated July 25 to commercial banks worth 17 billion Lebanese pounds.</p>
<p>The bank sold 60-day certificates worth 17 billion pounds at 12.25 percent annual interest. It said there was no demand for 45-day CDs.</p>
<p>Last week the bank sold 60-day certificates worth 31 billion pounds at 12.25 percent annual interest and made no sales of 45-day CDs at 11.5 percent.</p>
<p>($1 = 1,538 Lebanese pounds)</p>
<p>-Beirut editorial (9611) 345723 345740 602057</p>
